---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, contactHref } from '../../lib/site';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What personal information BidRadar collects, why, who processes it, and how to unsubscribe or delete your data."
  path="/privacy/"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="October 28, 2026"
>
  <p>
    BidRadar collects as little personal information as it can to send you a useful digest. This
    policy explains what we collect, why, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>When you sign up:</strong> your email address, and the trades and states you choose.
      We use these to build and send your digest.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you subscribe:</strong> our payment provider, Creem, collects your name, billing
      details and payment card. We receive confirmation of payment, your email address and basic
      billing information, never your full card number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you email us:</strong> the content of your message and your email address, so we
      can reply.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell, rent or share your email address with advertisers or list brokers.</li>
    <li>This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on a small number of service providers: a website host (the site is served as static
    pages, and the host may keep standard server logs such as IP address and browser type), an email
    delivery or form service that stores subscriber addresses and sends the digests, and Creem for
    payments. Each processes data only to provide its service to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Our emails</h2>
  <p>
    Every BidRadar email identifies us as the sender, includes our postal mailing address, and
    contains a clear unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing stops our emails right away, and always within
    10 business days. We send the digest only to people who asked for it.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your sign-up details while you receive our emails. If you unsubscribe and do not
    subscribe, we delete your trades and states within 90 days and keep only your email address on
    a suppression list so we never email you again by mistake. Payment records are kept as long as
    tax and accounting rules require.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us at any time to show you the information we hold about you, correct it, or delete
    it. Email <a href={contactHref}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will act on it within 30 days. Depending
    on where you live (for example California or the European Union), you may have additional rights
    under local law; we will honor them.
  </p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    BidRadar is operated from China, and our service providers may process data in the United States
    and other countries. We use providers that protect data with industry-standard security.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>BidRadar is a business service and is not directed to anyone under 16.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy we will update the date above, and tell subscribers by email about any
    significant change. Questions: <a href={contactHref}>{SITE.email}</a>, or {SITE.address.line1},
    {SITE.address.line2}, {SITE.address.line3}, {SITE.address.country}.
  </p>
</Page>
